<title>MEXICO: Mexico Cetes rise at central bank auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Cetes rise at central bank auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's benchmark 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity   Weighted Average     Change bps  Min rate  Max rate</p>
<p>  28-day	 20.90		 +5	     20.25    21.14</p>
<p>  91-day	 21.26		 +2	     21.24    21.29</p>
<p>  182-day	21.48		+19	     21.42    21.60</p>
<p>  343-day	22.08		+12	     22.00    22.11</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day peper was assigned at 22.20 percent.</p>
<p>    Maturity    Assigned    Demand		  Bid/Cover</p>
<p>    28-day	800 million	1.81 bln pesos	 2.26</p>
<p>    91-day	800 million	7.03 bln pesos	 8.79</p>
<p>    181-day     800 million	2.27 bln pesos	 2.84</p>
<p>    343-day     600 million	3.24 bln pesos	 5.40</p>
<p>The bid to the cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.78 on demand of 14.35 billion pesos compared with 4.1 the week before on demand of 12.3 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-day	    24 basis points</p>
<p>    91-day	    3 basis points</p>
<p>    181-day	   12 basis points</p>
<p>    343-day	   3 basis points</p>
<p>((--Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9565))</p>
